{"name":"Burning Bush","hex":"#a0403e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burning bush","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A biblical object described in Exodus 3:1-22, used by Yahweh to communicate with Moses.","Any plant of several species of Euonymus:\nA winged spindle or winged euonymus (Euonymus alatus), with vivid magenta Fall foliage, native to eastern Asia common as an ornamental and invasive in North America.\nA western burning bush (Euonymus occidentalis), native to western North America\nAn eastern burning bush (Euonymus atropurpureus), an ornamental shrub native to the midwestern US that bears a red berry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burning_bush"}],"entries":[{"title":"Burning bush","blocks":[{"text":"The burning bush refers to an event recorded in the Jewish Torah. It happened in the mid-15th century BCE or the 13th century BCE. It is described in the third chapter of the Book of Exodus as having occurred on Mount Horeb. According to the biblical account, the bush was on fire but was not consumed by the flames, hence the name. In the biblical and Quranic narrative, the burning bush is the location at which Moses was appointed by God to lead the Israelites out of Egypt and into Canaan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bourdon%2C_S%C3%A9bastien_-_Burning_bush.jpg/330px-Bourdon%2C_S%C3%A9bastien_-_Burning_bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_bush"},{"title":"Burning Bush (miniseries)","blocks":[{"text":"Burning Bush is a 2013 three-part miniseries created for HBO by Polish director Agnieszka Holland. Based on real characters and events, this haunting drama focuses on the personal sacrifice of a Prague history student, Jan Palach, who set himself on fire in 1969 in protest against the Soviet occupation of Czechoslovakia in the previous year. Dagmar Burešová, a young female lawyer, became part of his legacy by defending Palach's family in a trial against the communist government, a regime which tried to dishonour Palach’s sacrifice, a heroic action for the freedom of Czechoslovakia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/64/Burning_Bush_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burning_Bush_(miniseries)"},{"title":"Combustion","blocks":[{"text":"Combustion, or burning, is a high-temperature exothermic redox chemical reaction between a fuel and an oxidant, usually atmospheric oxygen, that produces oxidized, often gaseous products, in a mixture termed as smoke. Combustion does not always result in fire, because a flame is only visible when substances undergoing combustion vaporize, but when it does, a flame is a characteristic indicator of the reaction. While activation energy must be supplied to initiate combustion, the heat from a flame may provide enough energy to make the reaction self-sustaining. The study of combustion is known as combustion science."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Fire%2C_Fireplace%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Fire%2C_Fireplace%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combustion"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Moses_Dura_Europos.jpg/330px-Moses_Dura_Europos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Moses_Dura_Europos.jpg/330px-Moses_Dura_Europos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Moses and the burning bush. Painting from Dura-Europos synagogue, third century CE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoses_Dura_Europos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Bouts_moses.jpg/500px-Bouts_moses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Bouts_moses.jpg/1280px-Bouts_moses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Bouts_moses.jpg/500px-Bouts_moses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Moses and the Burning Bush, c. 1450–1475, attributed to Dieric Bouts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABouts_moses.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Moses_sinai_law.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Moses_sinai_law.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Icon of Moses receiving the Ten Commandments. The bush is depicted at his feet, lower left (Saint Catherine's Monastery, c. 1050)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoses_sinai_law.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Burning_Bush%2C_St_Catherine%27s_Monastery.jpg/500px-Burning_Bush%2C_St_Catherine%27s_Monastery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Burning_Bush%2C_St_Catherine%27s_Monastery.jpg/1280px-Burning_Bush%2C_St_Catherine%27s_Monastery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Burning_Bush%2C_St_Catherine%27s_Monastery.jpg/500px-Burning_Bush%2C_St_Catherine%27s_Monastery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The bush at Saint Catherine's Monastery in the Sinai Peninsula, which monastic tradition identifies as being the burning bush.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABurning_Bush%2C_St_Catherine's_Monastery.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Nicola_Froment%2C_Triptych_of_the_Burning_Bush%2C_1475%2C_Aix-en-Provence%2C_Church_Saint-Sauveur.jpg/500px-Nicola_Froment%2C_Triptych_of_the_Burning_Bush%2C_1475%2C_Aix-en-Provence%2C_Church_Saint-Sauveur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Nicola_Froment%2C_Triptych_of_the_Burning_Bush%2C_1475%2C_Aix-en-Provence%2C_Church_Saint-Sauveur.jpg/1280px-Nicola_Froment%2C_Triptych_of_the_Burning_Bush%2C_1475%2C_Aix-en-Provence%2C_Church_Saint-Sauveur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Nicola_Froment%2C_Triptych_of_the_Burning_Bush%2C_1475%2C_Aix-en-Provence%2C_Church_Saint-Sauveur.jpg/500px-Nicola_Froment%2C_Triptych_of_the_Burning_Bush%2C_1475%2C_Aix-en-Provence%2C_Church_Saint-Sauveur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Burning Bush Triptych, 1475-1476, by Nicolas Froment in Aix Cathedral","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANicola_Froment%2C_Triptych_of_the_Burning_Bush%2C_1475%2C_Aix-en-Provence%2C_Church_Saint-Sauveur.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Neopalimaya_kupina.jpg/250px-Neopalimaya_kupina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/Neopalimaya_kupina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Neopalimaya_kupina.jpg/250px-Neopalimaya_kupina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traditional icon of Our Lady of the Burning Bush (Neopalimaya Kupina).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AN